1
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:06,000
He just landed the gig of his life: 5th grade.

2
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:06,000
School of Rock is a comedy, music film directed by Richard Linklater.

3
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:06,000
Fired from his band and hard up for cash, guitarist and vocalist Dewey Finn finagles his way into a job as a fifth-grade
substitute teacher at a private school, where he secretly begins teaching his students the finer points of rock 'n' roll.

4
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:06,000
The school's hard-nosed principal is rightly suspicious of Finn's activities.

5
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:06,000
But Finn's roommate remains in the dark about what he's doing.

6
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Dewey Finn, played by Jack Black.

7
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:06,000
Rosalie Mullins, played by Joan Cusack.

8
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Ned Schneebly, played by Mike White.

9
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Patty Di Marco, played by Sarah Silverman.

10
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
Summer Hathaway, played by Miranda Cosgrove.

11
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
Zack, played by Joey Gaydos Jr..

12
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
School of Rock (titled on screen as The School of Rock) is a 2003 American comedy film
directed by Richard Linklater, produced by Scott Rudin and written by Mike White.

13
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
The film stars Jack Black, Joan Cusack, White and Sarah Silverman.

14
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
Black plays struggling rock guitarist Dewey Finn, who is fired from his band and
subsequently poses as a substitute teacher at a prestigious prep school.

15
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
After witnessing the musical talent of the students, Dewey forms a band of fifth-graders to
attempt to win the upcoming Battle of the Bands and use his winnings to pay his rent.

16
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
School of Rock was released on October 3, 2003, by Paramount Pictures,
grossing $131 million worldwide on a $35 million budget.

17
01:25:00,000 --> 01:25:06,000
The film received positive reviews from critics, with
praise for Black's performance and humor.

18
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
It was the highest-grossing music-themed comedy of all time
until the release of Pitch Perfect 2 in 2015.

19
01:35:00,000 --> 01:35:06,000
A stage musical adaptation opened on Broadway in December 2015, and a television
adaptation aired for three seasons on Nickelodeon from March 2016 to April 2018.

20
01:40:00,000 --> 01:40:06,000
The film explores themes of high school, rock 'n' roll,
musician, music competition, substitute teacher.

21
01:45:00,000 --> 01:45:06,000
The tone is lighthearted and dark.
